42
00:02:37,350 --> 00:02:40,260
So when the coin goes in, it measures that coin

43
00:02:40,261 --> 00:02:46,260
itself, decides if it's a true coin or not, and then decides where it's going to go from that point.

44
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:51,220
The comparator uses principles similar to that of a metal detector.

45
00:02:51,221 --> 00:02:56,860
The magnetic properties of incoming coins are compared to the properties of a reference coin.

46
00:02:57,860 --> 00:03:02,900
If the coin is deemed valid, it's routed through the machine and dropped into the hopper.

47
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:08,420
