71
00:04:31,260 --> 00:04:36,440
The slot machine, or one-armed bandit, was invented more than a century ago

72
00:04:36,441 --> 00:04:39,680
and quickly became a fixture in Western saloons.

73
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:44,440
But anti-gambling fervor led manufacturers to build machines

74
00:04:44,441 --> 00:04:47,220
that would dispense gum rather than cash.

75
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:49,640
Fruit and bar symbols on the reels

76
00:04:49,641 --> 00:04:51,580
determined what kind of gum was awarded.

77
00:04:52,380 --> 00:04:56,140
And before long, those symbols became a slot machine standard.

78
00:04:59,080 --> 00:05:01,380
Slots managed to survive prohibition,

79
00:05:02,180 --> 00:05:04,840
as well as crusading politicians,

80
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:08,980
by moving into speakeasies across the country.

81
00:05:08,981 --> 00:05:17,200
But in 1931, when Nevada legalized gambling, slot machines were back in the spotlight.

82
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:24,540
Mobster Bugsy Siegel installed them in his famous Flamingo Hotel to entertain the wives of high rollers.

83
00:05:25,500 --> 00:05:29,020
The machines soon became more profitable than the table games.

84
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:36,040
Today, nearly 70% of casino floor space is given over to slots.

85
00:05:36,041 --> 00:05:44,260
But the old one-armed bandits have been transformed into cutting-edge digital machines that no longer take coins.

86
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:49,940
